details={
9:('Read all 181 extracted lines, including the complete proof. Re-derived maximal-Cohen–Macaulay normalization/conductor biduality over the Gorenstein surface, the exact Q=omega_Gamma tensor omega_S^-1 comparison, chi(Gamma)=g(B)-1, support-connectedness under blowdowns with a=m-1, generic conductor length2 forcing degree1, and 2-g>=g forcing a smooth elliptic component. Checked the subsequent minimality and connected-Picard-image-in-two-points argument. The final duality is on the resulting smooth ruled normalization.', ['A.5.3','A.5.8','C2d','A.2.4'], ['RR70','AtiyahSinger1963'], []),
10:('Read all 227 lines. Independently checked both positions of the ruling tangent in the ordinary-cusp differential: its divisorial order is epsilon=0 or1 and total differential-minor order is1. For each vertical plane branch, the residual derivative order is m_i-1; missing coefficients u,...,u^(m_i-1) give delta>=m_i-1, Gorenstein conductor duality gives conductor exponent2delta, and other branches add intersection valuations, proving 2R<=V. Checked saturation/reflexivity and all zero-dimensional lengths; recomputed c2 identity L²+LM+M²=ell1+ell2 and both intersection polynomials. The epsilon=0 equality makes E locally free and supplies the actual nonzero T_C→N_C/Z map of degree -v. Negative semidefiniteness plus effectivity kills V,D_p; adjunction excludes a ruling (-1)-curve. The local conclusion uses checked A.5.7.', ['A.5.7'], ['RR70'], ['independent_chern_check.py']),
11:('Read all 156 lines. Checked descent of the ruling and the finite ambiguity set, the embedded tree collapse as a cofibration/homotopy equivalence, and the actual quotient map a:S→Sigma/J with a delta=q. Re-derived the barycentric-neighbourhood retraction for a full subcomplex, proper shrinking of the fibre tube, loop general position, and Z^4 semidirect Z→pi1(Sigma). Its metabelianity contradicts the explicit F2→S4 quotient for genus>=2. Opened Lojasiewicz1964 original §3 Theorem2 p464 and its precise compatibility conditions; compact complex-analytic (Y,S) is a permitted finite semianalytic family.', ['A.5.8'], ['Lojasiewicz1964'], []),
12:('Read all 128 lines. Re-derived canonical evaluation from the torsion-free rank-one f_*K_Y without imposing k=m-1; its zero divisor is kS and omega_S^m is trivial. HRR gives chi(O_S)=0; a section of a torsion line trivializes it on the compact reduced support. Nonconstant Picard pullback has nonzero differential through H1(S,O)→H1(T,O), bounding h0(Q)<=e. Rechecked nonreduced conductor CM duality and the H1 restriction surjection to each reduced component, followed by degree-zero curve Riemann–Roch and normalization delta. No lci or conductor-reducedness assumption was inserted.', ['A.5.9'], ['AtiyahSinger1963','RR70'], []),
13:('Read all 83 lines, plus the full E4 and D.1.9 extracted proofs needed here. The transgression gamma has nonzero image on each full fibre; natural base change therefore makes the section of the locally free rank-one R1O nowhere zero. HRR and coherent Leray force the torsion sheaf R2O to have length0. Checked top-degree base change and multiplication-by-parameter for the full-fibre dimensions, quotient to the reduced support, nonconstant Picard differential, H0(Q)=0, and the genus bound from conductor duality/degree-zero RR.', ['E4','D.1.9','A.5.9','A.5.12'], ['AtiyahSinger1963','RR70','BS76'], []),
16:('Read all 519 lines, including all post-proof minimal-model and negative-boundary derivations. Re-derived the conductor inclusion omega_T into the torsion ambient line, vanishing H2(T,O), and rationality/Leray proof of rational singularities. The branchwise-constant sheaf map V→Q is injective by equal values at a local image point; its natural connecting square proves complex coefficient-map injectivity. Checked effective anticanonical D, support equality including exceptional fibres, and Euler formula with the off-conductor correction retained until A.5.17 removes it. Recomputed every P2/F_n complement Euler entry and a=m-1 blowup change. Checked e(Gamma_red)>=0, including the elliptic-nodal image exclusion by the hypersurface branch intersection and extra graph path. For negative boundary classes, verified the actual topological pushout, metabelian quotient, and labelled nonbacktracking-walk obstruction to a one-component b1=1 image. No unrestricted Euler-sign conclusion is inferred from the finite tables.', ['A.5.3','A.5.9','A.5.12','A.5.17','A.5.11','D.1.9'], ['RR70','Lojasiewicz1964'], []),
18:('Read all 706 lines, including the final connected rational double-cover paragraph. Re-derived the quotient to the actual singular image D/J and beta<=1, then the two branch budgets and the three q cases. Verified the exact X shift/fourth-root coordinate change giving Y^4+X²Z at a smooth simple discriminant zero, and the no-pole refinement when the Hessian factor is a unit on every singular preimage. Checked the complete colength<=2 analytic-ring classification, actual ambient coordinates, symbolic squares by DVR residue dimensions/saturation, noncancellable Hessian determinant poles, conormal determinant defects6, and all transverse charts with fixed curve parameter. Product differentiation gives cubic/quartic pole bounds10/20,6/12,2/4 for arbitrary holomorphic coefficients, not only the sampled polynomials. Verified weighted-jet covariance, even-pole branch parity, and the negative degree/branch contradictions. The final minimal-resolution factorization, a=m-1 blowdown argument and Euler comparison were independently followed. All three cited exact scripts reran successfully; numerical case loops are corroboration of the displayed general inequalities, not a replacement for them.', ['A.5.5','A.5.8','A.5.11','A.5.14','A.5.15','A.5.17','C2d'], ['Lojasiewicz1964'], ['E_tacnode_bounds.py','E_low_delta_tacnode.py','A_low_delta_cusp.py']),
19:('Read all 277 lines, including the affine-product caution. Re-derived discriminant degree12-12delta for lci images. Checked the three analytic non-lci rings and every symbolic-cube identity: DVR residue dimension18 for the space cusp, direct primary-ideal intersection for cusp-plus-line, and the monomial inequalities for three axes. The normalized conormal degree4 and cubic pole totals3 imply corrected discriminant degree-12 in all cases. Rechecked that the finite tangent-root scheme is etale when delta=1, and that its generic algebra identifies the actual normalized conductor cover by integral closure, so every cover of P1 has degree1. The rational smooth-image degree2/3 cases remain explicitly unexcluded. Elliptic cleanup uses the already checked a=m-1 argument. Reran both cited exact programs, with byte-identical retained outputs.', ['A.5.5','A.5.14','A.5.18','C2d'], [], ['E_triple_images.py','A_low_delta_cusp.py']),
20:('Read all 76 lines. A generic cusp has one normalization branch, so the noncontracted section maps with degree1 to its image normalization; A.5.14/A.5.5 make the image smooth elliptic and the type constant. Checked the normalization parameter powers P²=R, P³=Q, which give degree0 of its normal line. Re-derived the minimal-resolution/ruling blowdown argument without assuming an initially smooth normalization, and the exact Euler comparison e(T)-e(C)+e(D)=0.', ['A.5.14','A.5.5','A.5.18','C2d'], [], []),
21:('Read all 277 lines, including both scalar-zero comparisons. Verified the exact weighted unit map and the connected cyclic projective cover of P=1; P(1,0)!=0 gives d distinct simple v-zeros. Followed the matching-circle sphere, parallel-arc push-off and endpoint linking signs, yielding square-2, and its shrinking embedding into a torus. For variable coefficients checked actual holomorphic factorization, unchanged critical axes, normal-gradient lower bound of order d-1 versus tangential order d, boundary submersion, proper analytic critical-value discriminant and connected complement, and oriented Ehresmann transport. Re-derived the two explicit scalar-zero coordinate/cover maps and the conductor orders in the aspherical warning model. The proof keeps its P(1,0) hypothesis. Exact programs reran successfully; the endpoint integer assertion in code alone is not treated as a topological proof.', ['A.5.15','A.5.17'], [], ['E_binary_products.py','E_cubic_double.py']),
}

